{"repositoryId":1424530821,"availability":"available","full":"kraewon7422/sketchlab","name":"sketchlab","description":"Sketch rough math figures with a pen and get clean, textbook-quality shapes back in place — a browser tool built for note-taking on tablets.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-18T15:39:06Z","updated":"2026-10-19T01:16:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kraewon7422.github.io/sketchlab/","topics":["geometry","handwriting-recognition","math-education","note-taking","pwa","react","s-pen","shape-recognition","sketch","stylus","svg","typescript"],"demo":"https://kraewon7422.github.io/sketchlab/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:48:57.540Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T11:48:57.540Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T11:48:57.540Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T11:48:57.540Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Sketch it rough with a pen; get a textbook-quality figure back, right where you drew it.","▶ Try it: kraewon7422.github.io/sketchlab. Draw a shape, then tap ✨ (or press Enter). On a tablet, finish a stroke and hold the pen still for half a second: that stroke snaps on its own. Tap the ƒ button to type an equation (y=x^2-3, y=a sin(bx), x^2+y^2=4, \\int0^2 x^2 dx) and get a textbook graph, or pick a 3D solid and turn it with your finger. Tap anything to copy it into your notes.","I take math and science notes by hand on a Galaxy Tab. Drawing a clean graph, a solid you can rotate, or a chemical structure inside a notes app is slow, and the usual workaround (plotting in Python and pasting the image) looks rough and isn't interactive at all."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kraewon7422/sketchlab/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a1dc0ab02bc02c513a568eebb4796d6693c9a644b2e1913fa26e6526baae0f65","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T11:48:57.644Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:48:5